    "type": "question",
    "label": "8",
    "prompt": "Differentiate $e^{\\sin x}$, and hence find $\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\cos x\\,e^{\\sin x}\\,dx$.",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$\\displaystyle\\frac{d}{dx}e^{\\sin x}=\\cos x\\,e^{\\sin x}$; $\\displaystyle\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\cos x\\,e^{\\sin x}\\,dx=e-1$.",
      "worked": "$$\\frac{d}{dx}e^{\\sin x}=\\cos x\\,e^{\\sin x}.$$\nHence\n$$\\begin{aligned}\\int_0^{\\pi/2}\\cos x\\,e^{\\sin x}\\,dx&=\\left[e^{\\sin x}\\right]_0^{\\pi/2}\\\\&=e^{\\sin(\\pi/2)}-e^{\\sin 0}\\\\&=e-1.\\end{aligned}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 28
